                            <comment id="16721201" author="sboikov" created="Fri, 14 Dec 2018 10:20:23 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It seems&#160;condition triggering test failure is small timeout for lock/put operations (it was 2 sec).&#160;On timeout test started to stop nodes while put/lock operations were in progress. When node is stopped then exchange future and all current update futures were completed with IgniteInterruptedCheckedException (GridCachePartitionExchangeManager.onKernalStop0), and this caused&#160;infinite loop in GridCacheAdapter.lockAll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;while&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;) {
    &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; {
        &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; fut.get();
    }
    &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; (IgniteInterruptedCheckedException ignored) {
        &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;// Interrupted status of current thread was cleared, retry to get lock.
&lt;/span&gt;        isInterrupted = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;;
    }
}&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I think it is not correct&#160;to complete operations with IgniteInterruptedCheckedException on node stop, so I changed it to use regular IgniteCheckedException.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I increased timeout in original test&#160;and added special test reproducing this hang.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Changes are in branch ignite-9213.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16721502" author="agoncharuk" created="Fri, 14 Dec 2018 15:07:42 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=sboikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;sboikov&quot;&gt;sboikov&lt;/a&gt;, can you attach a TC bot visa please?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16722508" author="sboikov" created="Sun, 16 Dec 2018 15:23:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoncharuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoncharuk&quot;&gt;agoncharuk&lt;/a&gt; I didn&apos;t manage to run TC bot for my branch, it seems it just doesn&apos;t work for branches, who can look at this issue?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16722851" author="dpavlov" created="Mon, 17 Dec 2018 10:26:02 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=sboikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;sboikov&quot;&gt;sboikov&lt;/a&gt; TC Bot does not support branches for automatic mode now, but it supports PRs. As a workaround, it is possible to create PR using branch in Apache git.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16722881" author="sboikov" created="Mon, 17 Dec 2018 11:07:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dpavlov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dpavlov&quot;&gt;dpavlov&lt;/a&gt;, are there any plans to support branches for TC Bot?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
